{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789556630,"nonce":"gMcR7zcxurMdhlDpT5Q2kHXohSA=","title":"Avoid boxed-constant initializer calls on every Python function entry","message":"IR audit of the checked float kernel shows __zyntax_box_constants() at the entry of float$Point$normalize and other frequently called Python methods. The generated Cranelift IR loads a reload-cell target and calls the initializer indirectly before doing direct f64 work; the initializer itself tests a global once flag. const_boxes::run_module inserts this call into every host entry. Determine whether constants can be initialized once at module load or the guard can be hoisted without breaking lazy imports, reload, or collector roots. Measure the checked float and nbody kernels before and after. This is a measured IR cost, not yet a measured runtime speedup.","files":null}]}